  "narrative": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">The dataset titled \"Genomic data for Ministeria vibrans, Parvularia atlantis, Pigoraptor vietnamica and Pigoraptor chileana\" has garnered early attention within the scholarly community, evidenced by its 6 citations and high visibility in reputable platforms such as Protist and eLife. This research contributes to the fields of metagenomics and evolutionary biology, underlining its relevance to sustainability, particularly in relation to terrestrial life.</p>\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Published in 2022 on Figshare, the dataset encapsulates genomic data pivotal for understanding the biological diversity of specific protist species. The work is characterized by its open-access nature, facilitating access for researchers and educators interested in computational biology and whole genome sequencing. Its alignment with the Sustainable Development Goal (SDG) pertaining to Life in Land further emphasizes its ecological significance.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">The dataset has witnessed an uptake in citations, with notable mentions stemming from high-impact venues, enhancing its visibility in areas related to biology and evolutionary studies. Researchers have engaged with this dataset in a variety of contexts, illustrated by its downstream reuse in articles and preprints, thus validating its relevance in ongoing scientific discussions.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">With a total of 136 views and 48 downloads recorded, the engagement metrics suggest a growing interest among the academic community. This interest is bolstered by its mention in prominent platforms designed for sharing preprints and academic articles, which are indicative of its potential to influence future research.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Additionally, future research utilizing this dataset may explore further ramifications in sustainability policies or climatic impacts on biodiversity, fostering conversations on ecological preservation. This initiative underlines the importance of open data in advancing scientific knowledge and public understanding of complex biological interactions.</p>",
